Task: Implement Resilience.middleware (Green) — real circuit-breaker bug found and fixed

Summary: Added Resilience.middleware composing Retry.middleware (outer) around
CircuitBreaker.middleware (inner), per resilience4j's documented recommended ordering.

Real bug found while making the composition test pass: CircuitBreaker.middleware
called breaker.onSuccess(...) for ANY Right(response) from the underlying client,
regardless of HTTP status — since a 5xx response is a normal returned VALUE (not a
thrown exception), it was being recorded as a SUCCESS, so the breaker could never
trip from 5xx responses at all, only from genuine exceptions. Fixed by configuring
resilience4j's CircuitBreakerConfig.recordResult(Predicate<Object>) to classify a 5xx
Response as a failure, and calling breaker.onResult(...) (which applies that
predicate) instead of onSuccess(...) for the Right(response) branch.

Files changed:
- modules/purerest/src/main/scala/purerest/resilience/Resilience.scala (new)
- modules/purerest/src/main/scala/purerest/resilience/CircuitBreaker.scala (bug fix)

Verified: full purerest/test suite green (23/23), including both new ResilienceSuite
scenarios — the second of which is exactly what caught this bug on first run.
